menu "WiFi configuration"

config WIFI_SSID
    string "Default WiFi SSID"
    default ""
    help
        Fallback used only if no credentials have been saved via the
        'wifi_set <ssid> <password>' console command (NVS always wins once
        set). Leave blank to require the console command instead.

config WIFI_PASSWORD
    string "Default WiFi password"
    default ""
    help
        See CONFIG_WIFI_SSID. Stored in plaintext in the built binary like
        any other Kconfig string -- fine for a bring-up default, but prefer
        the console command for anything you don't want sitting in flash.

config MDNS_HOSTNAME
    string "mDNS hostname (reachable as <hostname>.local)"
    default "phone"
    help
        Advertised over mDNS once WiFi is up -- resolvable as e.g.
        "phone.local" from macOS/iOS (native Bonjour), Linux (needs avahi,
        usually already installed), and Windows 10+ (native) or older
        Windows with Bonjour Print Services installed.

endmenu
